coder › Done. Implemented on `work/main`, committed as `6c0d18a`.

What changed:
- `src/store.ts`
  - Added `markDone(todos, id)`: throws `RangeError` (`no such todo: <id>`) when no todo has the id; otherwise returns a new array with the matching todo's `done` set to `true`. The input list is not mutated.
  - Updated `render` so `list` shows `[x]` for done todos and `[ ]` for the rest, e.g. `[x] 1. buy milk`.
- `src/cli.ts`
  - Added the `done <id>` command. A non-whole-number id or an id no todo has prints `error: <id>` and exits with code `1`, leaving `todos` unchanged (the same reference is returned). A valid id prints `done: <text>` with code `0`.
  - Updated the usage line to include `done <id>`.
- Tests
  - `src/store.test.ts` (new): `markDone` returns a new list with the right todo done, doesn't mutate input, and throws `RangeError` naming the id.
  - `src/cli.test.ts`: command tests for success, non-whole-number id, unknown id, and the `[x]`/`[ ]` list rendering.

Decisions the plan left open:
- List line format is `[x] 1. buy milk` (checkbox before the existing `id. text`).
- Error lines are exactly `error: <id>` (the raw argument), which starts with `error:` and names the id.

